        "title": "Configurable Chromium executable for managed browsers on Desktop",
        "summary": "Desktop users can now point Aura's managed browser at a specific Chromium binary, with the choice persisted across launches and surfaced in Advanced settings.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Introduced persisted browser runtime settings so a user-chosen Chromium executable path is loaded from disk at startup and merged with environment-based CDP configuration, with the executable and its source logged during backend initialization.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "a1cd3b171c66a532aca81598e289649e58002f3b"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Added a new /api/browser-executable endpoint on the desktop app to read and update the managed browser path, including validation that returns a 400 on bad input and reports the resolved status back to the UI.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "a1cd3b171c66a532aca81598e289649e58002f3b"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Built out the Advanced section of Settings with UI for viewing and changing the managed browser executable, backed by new desktop API bindings and tests.",
